    fix(interruptor): state the real scope of the world-writable-path block (DF-TERMINAL-JAIL-7)
    
    The `builtin-chmod-777-root` block message and description claimed the rule
    scopes to root ("Setting world-writable permissions on root (/) is blocked"),
    while the pattern's target is `\s+/` — it fires on ANY absolute /-rooted path.
    A live probe blocked `chmod 777 /tmp/tjprobe/work` with that root-only reason.
    
    Message (plugin/terminal_jail/interruptor/blocklist.py +
    plugin/terminal_jail/rules/00-builtins.yaml, byte-identical text):
    - names the refused shape: chmod making a path world-writable (777 / 7777 /
      a+rwx, `-R`/`--recursive` optional),
    - names the scope that actually fires: any absolute (/-rooted) target
      (/tmp/work, /var/www, /etc), not only root (/),
    - states that relative and ~-rooted targets keep their ALLOW verdict,
    - names the documented override: a same-id user rule in
      ~/.config/terminal-jail/rules.d/ set to warn level.
    - description: "World-writable root" -> "World-writable absolute path".
    
    Id, pattern, priority and action are untouched — rule behaviour is unchanged
    and re-probed: `chmod 777 /`, `chmod -R 777 /`, `chmod --recursive 777 /`,
    `chmod a+rwx /`, `chmod 7777 /`, `chmod -R 777 /etc` still block under
    `builtin-chmod-777-root`; `chmod 777 tjwork`, `chmod 777 ~/tjwork` and
    `chmod 755 /` still allow.
    
    Test: plugin/test_interruptor.py::test_block_messages_state_shape_and_scope
    gains `builtin-chmod-777-root` needles (chmod, 7777, a+rwx, recursive,
    absolute, relative, ~/, rules.d, warn level); the pre-fix root-only message
    fails them (RED verified by reverting only the message).
    
    Docs: README.md, specs/interruptor.md (real pattern + accurate reason),
    specs/integration.md and skills/terminal-jail-usage/SKILL.md pitfall #1 no
    longer present `chmod 777 /` as the rule's full scope.
    
    Gates: `.venv/bin/python -m pytest plugin -q` -> 821 passed, 5 skipped;
    `uvx ruff check .` -> All checks passed.
    
    Co-authored-by: Alexis Okuwa <wojonstech@gmail.com>
